{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,25]],"date-time":"2026-10-25T05:21:46Z","timestamp":1792905706268,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":56,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"9","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2012,8,3]],"date-time":"2012-08-03T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1343952000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2012,8,3]],"date-time":"2012-08-03T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1343952000000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/doi.wiley.com\/10.1002\/tdm_license_1.1"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2012,8,3]],"date-time":"2012-08-03T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1343952000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Macromolecular Bioscience"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2012,9]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    We report the structure\u2013activity relationship in the antimicrobial activity of linear and branched poly(ethylene imine)s (L\u2010 and B\u2010PEIs) with a range of molecular weights (MWs) (500\u201312\u2009000). Both L\u2010 and B\u2010PEIs displayed enhanced activity against\n                    <jats:italic>Staphylococcus aureus<\/jats:italic>\n                    over\n                    <jats:italic>Escherichia coli<\/jats:italic>\n                    . Both B\u2010 and L\u2010PEIs did not cause any significant permeabilization of\n                    <jats:italic>E. coli<\/jats:italic>\n                    cytoplasmic membrane. L\u2010PEIs induced depolarization of\n                    <jats:italic>S. aureus<\/jats:italic>\n                    membrane although B\u2010PEIs did not. The low MW B\u2010PEIs caused little or no hemolysis while L\u2010PEIs are hemolytic. The low MW B\u2010PEIs are less cytotoxic to human HEp\u20102 cells than other PEIs. However, they induced significant cell viability reduction after 24 h incubation. The results presented here highlight the interplay between polymer size and structure on activity.\n                    <jats:boxed-text content-type=\"graphic\" position=\"anchor\">\n                      <jats:graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1999\/xlink\" mimetype=\"image\/jpeg\" position=\"anchor\" specific-use=\"enlarged-web-image\" xlink:href=\"graphic\/mgra001.jpg\">\n                        <jats:alt-text>magnified image<\/jats:alt-text>\n                      <\/jats:graphic>\n                    <\/jats:boxed-text>\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/mabi.201200052","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2012,8,3]],"date-time":"2012-08-03T15:06:56Z","timestamp":1344006416000},"page":"1279-1289","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":249,"title":["Poly(ethylene imine)s as Antimicrobial Agents with Selective Activity"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"12","author":[{"given":"Katherine A.","family":"Gibney","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Iva","family":"Sovadinova","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Analette I.","family":"Lopez","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Michael","family":"Urban","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Zachary","family":"Ridgway","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Gregory A.","family":"Caputo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Kenichi","family":"Kuroda","seq